{title: A Future and a Hope}
{subtitle: Jeremiah 29:11}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 71}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] |
| [Dm/F] | [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Far from [Bb]home by a foreign river
[Gm]Hung my harp on the willow tree
[Eb]Every road I knew was broken
Every dream was lost [Fsus4]to me
Then a let[Bb]ter came one dusty morning
Build your [Gm]house and plant the vine
Seek the peace [Eb]of the city you live in
I have not for[F7sus4]gotten mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I hold the thoughts I [F]think [Bb]of you
Thoughts of peace and not [Gm7]of harm
A future and a hope, [Eb]my child
Held forever in my [F7sus4]arms
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Seventy years is [Bb]a long time waiting
Children grow and the old ones sigh
[Gm7]But the One who counts the sparrows
[Eb]Writes tomorrow in the sky
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F7sus4]I hold the thoughts I think of you
[Bb]Thoughts of peace and not of harm
[Gm7]A future and a hope, my child
[Eb]Held forever in my arms [F7sus4]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]When you [Eb]seek me, you will find me
[Bb]When you search [Eb]with all your heart
[Gm7]I will bring you home again
I will [Gm7]mend the broken parts
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]I hold the thoughts I think of [Fsus4]you
[F][Bb]Thoughts of peace and not of harm
A [Gm7]future and a hope, my child
Held [Eb]forever in my arms
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]A future [Bb]and a hope
A fu[Gm7]ture and a hope
[Eb]Peace and not harm [Fsus4]
A [Bb]future and [Gm7]a hope
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
